<!--
  maaaaaaxx.github.io/website

  Long-form pages, each written to stand on its own. There was an install
  guide once, and it was removed because redm.thepub.beer publishes one
  covering the same ground: two hosts carrying the same article compete with
  each other and one of them loses. Priorities are relative within this site
  only.

  Five subjects live here now - RedM, game clip recording, deckbuilding
  roguelikes, voxel terrain and Twitch chat bots - and they do not share a
  reader. They are kept apart rather than cross-linked: each page carries its
  own stylesheet, its own site name and its own disclosure, and no page links
  sideways to an unrelated one. Mixing them in a navigation would muddy what
  each page is about for no gain to any of them. The only shared link is the
  studio, which is a factual statement of who publishes them, not a promotion.

  The host in every <loc> must match the GitHub Pages URL exactly, including
  the trailing slash on the index and the lowercase name in /website/. A project
  page's path is case sensitive, so /Website/ is a 404 on this repository: the
  repo was renamed from Website to website and 57 references had to follow it.
  If this site ever moves to a custom domain, this file, the canonical tag on
  every page and the Sitemap line in robots.txt all change together, or
  Search Console reports the sitemap as containing URLs on a different host
  and ignores it.

  Submit at https://search.google.com/search-console for the github.io
  property, and at Bing Webmaster Tools. Resubmitting after adding pages is
  not required - Google re-reads the sitemap on its own schedule - but it is
  the fastest way to get new URLs into the crawl queue.
-->
